    "answer_text": "Chicken Tikka Masala\nChicken thigh, boneless: 900 g\nUnsweetened coconut yoghurt: 250 g\nCreme fraiche: 150 g\nTinned plum tomatoes: 400 g\nBrown onion: 250 g\nNeutral oil or vegan butter alternative: 50 g\nGinger, grated: 25 g\nGarlic, crushed: 20 g\nGaram masala: 10 g\nGround turmeric: 5 g\nKashmiri chilli powder: 8 g\nFine sea salt: 12 g\nKasoori methi: 4 g\nswap Full fat yoghurt -> Unsweetened coconut yoghurt (Provides the necessary acidity and creamy texture for the marinade without dairy.)\nswap Double cream -> Creme fraiche (Cultured, so it is gentler than cream and suits a dairy-free sauce.)\nswap Ghee -> Neutral oil or vegan butter alternative (Provides the fat needed for sautéing aromatics without using dairy-based ghee.)\n## Method\n\nMarinate the chicken in the yoghurt with half the ginger, garlic and spices for at least\nfour hours, ideally overnight. The acid in the yoghurt does the tenderising; more than\ntwenty-four hours and the texture turns mealy.\n\nThread onto skewers and grill hard until the edges char in places. You want colour, not\ndoneness — the pieces finish in the sauce.\n\nSoften the onion in the ghee, add the remaining ginger, garlic and spices, then the tomatoes.\nCook until thick and glossy, blend smooth, and return to the pan. Add the grilled chicken\nand simmer for ten minutes, then stir in the cream and the crushed kasoori methi off the\nheat.\nChicken thigh, boneless, Tinned plum tomatoes, Brown onion, Ginger, grated, Garlic, crushed, Garam masala, Ground turmeric, Kashmiri chilli powder, Fine sea salt, Kasoori methi. Using coconut-based products will introduce a subtle coconut flavor to the dish. Ensure your vegan butter alternative is certified dairy-free, as some brands may contain trace dairy ingredients. Chicken thigh, boneless, Tinned plum tomatoes, Brown onion, Ginger, grated, Garlic, crushed, Garam masala, Ground turmeric, Kashmiri chilli powder, Fine sea salt, Kasoori methi are all dairy-free."
